"""Package Aqua v12 / Test 4, main finisher411 and airborne dodge504."""
from pathlib import Path
import csv,hashlib,json,shutil,sys,zipfile,struct
from aqua_v12_plan import SETS,BANK,AIR_ALIASES
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
DEST=ROOT/'KH1FM_Aqua_Animation_Test_v12'
def sha(p):return hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()

README="KH1FM AQUA ANIMATION TEST v12 - TEST 4\nSteam Global / OpenKH Panacea\n\nMAIN AQUA\n- Air combo: 407, 352, 353 (first, second, finisher).\n- Aerial dodge: 504 on a fresh Circle press while jumping/falling, with either\n  neutral or directional left-stick input. The previous neutral-stick gate\n  is removed. Release the takeoff button, then press Circle again in the air.\n  It remains once per airtime; landing rearms it. Numbered entries inherit it.\n- Ground finisher411, normal falling506, Fire316/391, Thunder317/390,\n  Cure318/427, LEFT-hand spell origins/glow and wrist/hair corrections remain.\n\nTEST 4 ABILITIES - ALL 0 AP\naqua   : main ground combo300/301/302/411; air407/352/353; airborne504\naqua 1 : ground622 623 045 ; air220 221 351\naqua 2 : ground353 399 411 ; air413 710 711\naqua 3 : ground060 022 023 ; air025 026 052\naqua 4 : ground701 700 708 ; air007 / 395, 008 / 051, 060 / 505\n\nThe slash pairs are aliases for identical animation data, not alternate picks.\nThe shared versions are selected as395 (29 source frames),051 (16 frames),\nand505 (30 frames). These are distinct from the ordinary007/008 base clips.\nPlain60 in aqua3 uses the separate40-frame060 from p02ex_711.arc. The4th air\nfinisher060 /505 uses the30-frame shared payload. Source hashes and exact\nbanks are recorded in TEST_CLIP_SOURCES.csv and source/source_selections.json.\n\nEach triplet is attack one, attack two, finisher. KH1's alternate second ground\nattack uses the selected second clip too. Numbered entries share the main\nmovement/casting/reaction/Guard/Cartwheel poses; only their combos differ.\nSelect one Aqua entry while idle; the other Aqua entries turn off. Native\nability states and ids117..121 are retained, including saved selections.\n\nINSTALL\n1. Fully close KH1.\n2. Disable Aqua v11 and all older Aqua packages, Sora Restore Check and\n   Nine Styles / Dual Wield. Keep other Sora model/moveset replacements off.\n3. Import this ZIP into OpenKH and enable Aqua Animation Test v12.\n4. Build and Run, then load your save.\n5. Equip aqua or one of aqua1..4 while idle. Missing entries are granted off;\n   saved selections are respected. Native entries are never evicted to fit.\n\nTEST ORDER\n- Equip aqua and test the407/352/353 air combo. Its ground finisher stays411.\n- Jump, release Circle, then tap Circle again. Check504 with no stick input,\n  while moving forward/back/left/right and while moving diagonally. Land to\n  rearm between tests. The native direction vector is passed through unchanged.\n- Check return to506 falling, landing and interruption by attacking/casting.\n- Equip aqua1..4 while idle; test their ground and air triplets. For a clean\n  test, unequip Slapshot, Sliding Dash, Vortex, Hurricane Blast and other\n  native combo replacements. Their separate actions keep their native poses.\n- Recheck spells and LEFT-hand effects, both saves, room transitions/reloads,\n  then turn every Aqua entry off and check native Sora controls and poses.\n\nAERIAL DODGE SCOPE\nThis remains an animation test using the existing40-frame fall record.\n504 plays once, then restores506. It keeps native air steering, gravity,\nvelocity and collisions; no BBS dash/boost, hitbox or invulnerability is added.\nA held takeoff button does not retrigger it. Attacks/casts/reactions, ledges,\nscene/menu/shortcut input and other busy actions do not start it. Guard and\nDodge Roll still need their native abilities;504 needs no extra native ability.\nA fresh moving-air Circle now takes the504 route too. If you keep Circle held\npast the pose, KH1 may then enter its native Glide. Glide's poses stay native.\n\nRETURN\nReturn the NEW kh1-aqua.log beside the game EXE and a short video. Its first\nline must say ANIMATION TEST v12 Test 4. AIR DODGE READY confirms hook admission;\nAIR DODGE504 confirms a trigger with neutral or directional input. If it says\nAIR DODGE UNAVAILABLE, other Aqua poses remain available with native air input.\nProfile values:0 native,1 aqua,2 aqua1,3 aqua2,4 aqua3,5 aqua4.\nCHECK_AQUA_V12.cmd optionally checks installation hashes and writes\nAqua_Animation_Check_v12.txt.\n\nLAYOUT / CASTING\nBoth installed MSETs are original. All generated poses keep native headers,\nlengths, table allocations, bone counts, eleven helpers and native travel.\nUnknown/foreign motion data or request tables block writes. Only the supplied\nnormal Sora and Olympus banks are admitted. KH1 damage, native hit events,\nspell scripts/MP/targeting, Guard coverage and Dodge Roll windows remain.\nBBS command logic/effects/damage are not imported with these source clips.\nThunder retains v10's separated casting lookup and86 ground/78 air frames\nrather than68/68. Blizzard/Gravity share317/390; Stop/Aero318/427. That inherited\ncast timing still needs an in-game check. Unequipping restores native lookup\npointers and mapped body records when the current action finishes at idle.\n\nFILE GUIDE\nABILITY_SETS.txt lists Test4 sequences.\nANIMATION_MAP.csv lists the usual motions for all five profiles.\nAIR_DODGE_MAPPING.csv lists the temporary504 action and input rule.\nTEST_CLIP_SOURCES.csv lists main combo/dodge and Test4 sources, frame counts,\naliases and payload hashes; source/source_selections.json records inventory choices.\nThe unchanged349-clip inventory is under inventory. Current assignments are\nin this package's mapping files. Numeric IDs are not official command names.\n\nOPTIONAL FALLBACKS\nTo disable only the airborne Circle action, copy\nDISABLE_AIR_DODGE_kh1-aqua.ini beside the EXE as kh1-aqua.ini and restart.\nThe main air combo, ground finisher, Test4 sets, fall506 and magic remain.\nTo retain native weapon-tip spell attachments, use\nDISABLE_HAND_MAGIC_kh1-aqua.ini instead. Combine air_dodge=0 and hand_magic=0\nin one [aqua] INI if needed. Remove the INI and restart to restore defaults.\n\nREMOVE ALL AQUA ENTRIES\nCopy REMOVE_AQUA_kh1-aqua.ini beside the EXE as kh1-aqua.ini. Leave v12 enabled,\nrestart and load each save to clean. Check AQUA ABILITIES REMOVED, then save\nin-game. Exit, remove the INI, disable v12 and rebuild. Only ids117..121 are\nremoved; native ability order stays intact.\n\nVALIDATION\n50 tests execute the emitted PE DLL in a Win64 ABI mock host. They cover\nneutral/directional Circle, unchanged direction/input data, one use per airtime,\nheld-button and busy-action exclusions, interruptions, body/lookup restoration,\nall five profiles/both banks, native detours/trampolines and failure paths.\n14 geometry/assignment tests cover all76 pose variants, exact Test4 triplets,\nslash-alias hashes and distinct plain060, native capacities/travel, bind lengths\nand scales, hair, wrists and retained jump/Fire transitions. All fits remain\nbelow the existing5-unit position-error limit; no capacity expansion is used.\nThese checks do not run Windows/KH1 or render Sora's mesh. The directional\nCircle route, new clips and final pose/FX appearance need in-game testing.\n"

SOURCE="AQUA V12 TEST 4 SOURCE\n\nNormal installation requires OpenKH/Panacea; these are development files.\n\nDLL BUILD / EXECUTION CHECK (Linux x64)\n  python3 generate_data.py\n  python3 build.py\n  python3 test_runtime.py\n  python3 test_visuals.py\nGCC, GNU ld with i386pep support and Python are needed. Geometry checks also\nneed NumPy/SciPy. Runtime tests map the final PE and execute its real exports\nand attachment detours against Win64 ABI mocks, not Windows or KH1.\n\nREBUILD POSES (optional; NumPy, SciPy, Pillow)\nFrom this source directory:\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 0 --output .\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 1 --output sets/p1\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 2 --output sets/p2\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 3 --output sets/p3\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 4 --output sets/p4\n  python3 retargeting/tools/build_aqua_complete_v12.py --profile 5 --output dodge\n  python3 generate_data.py\n  python3 build.py\n  python3 test_runtime.py\n  python3 test_visuals.py\n--slots followed by normal slot numbers rebuilds only those records in a\nprofile. Required source ARC files are in retargeting/core_source. Original\nMSET files are ../assets. Immutable baseline sampling caches are reproducible\nand are not distributed. V9 anatomical refinements are retained and applied once to each baseline.\n\nANATOMICAL WRIST PIVOTS\naqua_refine_v9.py keeps Sora's distal forearm helper angles at bind and applies\nthe hand's authored orientation at pivots100/205. Arm solves rotate the whole\ndistal forearm together and preserve the hand's orientation at that pivot.\nArm clearance includes interior arm samples. The new main ground finisher411\nuses the normal correction envelope; the old304 finisher is no longer selected. All local anatomical\noffsets/scales retain their bind values. The V8 reference contains 41 samples\nof ten joints per original converted motion; it supports an independent\nbounded-displacement checks for unchanged source actions only. New casts,\nfalling, finisher411 and the407/352/353 main air combo are excluded from that historical comparison. It is not mesh\ncollision detection. Hair155..193 retains the v8 bind-rest correction.\n\nFIVE PROFILE GATE\nThe generated header stores original tables and five immutable after sets.\nUnchanged profile blocks are shared. All 47/46 records are admitted against\nthe known original/base/test sets before any writes. Selection changes wait\nfor idle. Ability ids117..121 are 0 AP. Newly enabled Aqua entries win and\nonly other Aqua entries are turned off. Missing entries are granted only if\nall fit with a terminator in the original 48-byte list. Native entries are\nnot evicted. Uninstall removes only ids117..121.\n\nAIRBORNE AERIAL DODGE\nThe main plan remains47 normal /46 Olympus records. Profile5 of the retargeting\nbuilder is a single non-looped504 variant of the existing fall record10.\ngenerate_data.py stores this as AquaPart.dodge; admission accepts it and the\nfast cache recognizes it only while the transient action is active.\naqua_air_dodge.h hooks Steam control0x2A6220 after exact17-byte admission. Its\ntrampoline copies the first10 bytes and rewrites the RIP-relative security-\ncookie load as mov rax, imm64; mov rax,[rax], targeting original0x554A88.\nThe original control, can-act0x297870 and queued-motion0x29F980 bytes are\nverified before installation. The last two functions are called, not hooked.\nFresh merged logical Jump/Circle bits6, any valid stick direction, free air1/2,\nheight>1, an admitted body bank and no busy/native queued action authorize504.\nOne use per airtime, armed after button release. Beginning from fall6 resets\nonly actor+16C to zero; beginning from rise queues native fall6. Native state,\nvelocity/gravity, collision and defense flags stay untouched. The control\ncall temporarily masks only Jump bits at pad+4/+8/+10/+14, then restores those\nbits without undoing native changes to other buttons. Clock39, looping,\nlanding or interruption restores the normal506 pose. Unknown/unloaded records\nare never restored by writing stale pointers. The action adds no invulnerability.\nThe native clock remains authoritative; waiting for a queued fall is bounded.\nair_dodge_validation.json records original executable evidence. The test host\nexecutes the real detour/trampoline and native can-act bytes; native queue and\ncontrol bodies are mocked. Actual Windows/KH1 testing remains outstanding.\n\nACTION CAST LOOKUP\nNative Steam command handlers dispatch ground magic with 0x36+spell and air\nmagic with 0x83+spell. Thunder is index2, Cure index3. The supplied MSETs share\ntheir physical record. aqua_cast_requests.h changes actor+1D8 to an immutable\n1408-byte request copy while a verified Aqua profile is active. Only Thunder\nmoves to the alternate casting family (normal55/80, Olympus18/42); all other\nrequest words and native flags remain. The original table is never written.\nNative resolver0x2A01E0 reads that field (+8 from actor+1D0). All body and\nrequest destinations must pass admission before writes; idle-only switching,\nper-bank original pointers, foreign-pointer rejection and exact restoration\nare tested. cast_request_validation.json records native instruction evidence\nfrom the supplied executable. No new entry-point detour is used here.\nThunder therefore uses 86 ground / 78 air frames, instead of the shared\n68/68 frames. Native per-record event tracks stay intact. Final spell timing\nhas not been tested in KH1. Blizzard/Gravity inherit317/390; Stop/Aero318/427.\n\nLEFT-HAND MAGIC\nThe two native entry points and admitted instruction spans are unchanged from\nv8. Their direct matrix selector is now0x20CE, the LEFT palm206, in all five\nprofiles. Native cast requests, current actor/bank, event/script exclusions\nand native fallthrough are retained. No spell-resource or projectile script\nis replaced. The supplied executable is not included; its original hash and\nthe entry spans are in native_attachment_validation.json.\n\nCAPACITY / SOURCE IDS\nNo motion/header/table expansion is used. The cast lookup copy has the original\n352 request words; only Thunder entries0x38/0x85 change their physical slot. The original eleven helpers and\nnative travel remain. Four sets change seven physical combo records each:\nC8 first, C9/CA second, CB finisher, CC first air, CD second air, CE finisher.\nThe donor selection is in aqua_v12_plan.py. Numeric IDs retain their exact\nsource bank/hash in TEST_CLIP_SOURCES.csv; no command names are inferred.\nThe source inventory files under ../inventory retain v8's source metadata.\nCurrent ability mappings are ../ANIMATION_MAP.csv.\n\nExisting upstream licenses and notices are retained in licenses.\nFormat reference: https://openkh.dev/bbs/file/type/pam.html\n\nTEST4 SOURCE VARIANTS\nNew requests carry source_sha256 and validate the exact selected PAM payload\nbefore fitting. The sampling-cache name includes this identity. Aliases395,\n051 and505 use the shared007/395,008/051 and060/505 inventory rows. Plain060\nuses the separate40-frame p02ex_711.arc payload;052 uses the20-frame gameplay\nclip. Prefer dedicated gameplay variants for045,353,399 and411. Required ARC\nfiles, including xaa*.arc banks, are in retargeting/core_source. Exact choices\nare source_selections.json; current assignments are the root mapping CSVs.\n"

def build():
    d=ROOT/'ability_v12';runtime=json.loads((d/'runtime_validation.json').read_text());geometry=json.loads((d/'visual_validation.json').read_text())
    reports=[json.loads((d/'curve_validation.json').read_text())]+[json.loads((d/f'sets/p{i}/curve_validation.json').read_text()) for i in range(1,5)]
    dodge=json.loads((d/'dodge/curve_validation.json').read_text())
    assert runtime['passed'] and geometry['passed'] and all(r['passed'] for r in reports+[dodge])
    shutil.copytree(ROOT/'KH1FM_Aqua_Animation_Test_v11',DEST,dirs_exist_ok=True)
    for name in ['CHECK_AQUA_V11.cmd','Check_Aqua_Animations_v11.ps1','source/arm_alignment_validation.json']:(DEST/name).unlink(missing_ok=True)
    for n in ['aqua.c','aqua_magic.h','aqua_cast_requests.h','aqua_air_dodge.h','aqua_data.h','build.py','generate_data.py','test_runtime.py','test_bridge.c','test_visuals.py',
              'curve_validation.json','data_validation.json','runtime_validation.json','visual_validation.json','cast_request_validation.json','air_dodge_validation.json','source_selections.json']:
        shutil.copy2(d/n,DEST/'source'/n)
    for name in ['fixtures','sets','dodge']:shutil.copytree(d/name,DEST/'source'/name,dirs_exist_ok=True)
    shutil.copy2(d/'kh1-aqua.dll',DEST/'dll/kh1-aqua.dll')
    for n in ['build_aqua_complete_v12.py','aqua_v12_plan.py','package_aqua_v12.py']:shutil.copy2(ROOT/'tools'/n,DEST/'source/retargeting/tools'/n)
    for name in sorted(set(BANK.values())):
        shutil.copy2(d/'source_arcs'/name,DEST/'source/retargeting/core_source'/name)
    (DEST/'README_FIRST.txt').write_text(README);(DEST/'source/README_SOURCE.txt').write_text(SOURCE)
    manifest=(ROOT/'KH1FM_Aqua_Animation_Test_v11/mod.yml').read_text();a=manifest.index('description:');b=manifest.index('assets:')
    desc='Test 4: main aqua air407/352/353 and airborne Circle dodge504 with neutral or directional stick input. Four new combo test sets with verified aliases; retains finisher411, fall506, action casts and LEFT-hand magic. Steam Global / Panacea; disable older Aqua packages and Nine Styles / Dual Wield.'
    manifest=manifest[:a]+'description: >-\n  '+desc+'\n'+manifest[b:]
    (DEST/'mod.yml').write_text(manifest.replace('Animation Test v11','Animation Test v12'))
    checker=(ROOT/'KH1FM_Aqua_Animation_Test_v11/Check_Aqua_Animations_v11.ps1').read_text().replace('v11','v12').replace('CHECK_AQUA_V11','CHECK_AQUA_V12')
    (DEST/'Check_Aqua_Animations_v12.ps1').write_text(checker)
    (DEST/'CHECK_AQUA_V12.cmd').write_bytes(b'@echo off\r\nsetlocal\r\npowershell.exe -NoLogo -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "%~dp0Check_Aqua_Animations_v12.ps1" %*\r\npause\r\n')
    (DEST/'REMOVE_AQUA_kh1-aqua.ini').write_text('[aqua]\nremove_aqua=1\nhand_magic=0\nair_dodge=0\n')
    (DEST/'DISABLE_HAND_MAGIC_kh1-aqua.ini').write_text('[aqua]\nremove_aqua=0\nhand_magic=0\nair_dodge=1\n')
    (DEST/'DISABLE_AIR_DODGE_kh1-aqua.ini').write_text('[aqua]\nremove_aqua=0\nhand_magic=1\nair_dodge=0\n')
    labels=['aqua']+[f'aqua {i}' for i in range(1,5)]
    (DEST/'ABILITY_SETS.txt').write_text('\n'.join([f'Ability {label} / id{117+i} / 0 AP' + (' / main air407 352 353; ground finisher411; airborne dodge504' if not i else f' / ground {" ".join(SETS[i-1][0])} / air {" ".join(SETS[i-1][1])}') for i,label in enumerate(labels)])+'\n\nSelect one while idle. Airborne504 accepts neutral or directional input in all five. Aqua4 air aliases:007/395,008/051,060/505.\n')
    maps=[];sources=[];airmaps=[]
    sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'tools'));from bbs_source_inspector import read_arc,read_pam
    for profile in range(5):
        active={r['normal_slot']:r for r in reports[0]['motions']}
        if profile:active.update({r['normal_slot']:r for r in reports[profile]['motions']})
        for r in sorted(active.values(),key=lambda r:r['normal_slot']):
            maps.append({'Ability':labels[profile],'Ability id':117+profile,'Action':r['action'],'Native request':f'0x{r["request"]:02X}',
              'Normal slot':r['normal_slot'],'Olympus slot':r['olympus_slot'] if r['olympus_slot']!=0xffffffff else 'not present',
              'Aqua clip':r['donor'],'Source aliases':r.get('source_aliases',''),'Source bank':r['source_bank'],'Source frame range':str(r['source_range']) if r['source_range'] else 'full',
              'Pose loop':r['loop'],'Native frames':r['native_frames'],'Root policy':r['root']})
        airmaps.append({'Ability':labels[profile],'Ability id':117+profile,'Action':'Aerial dodge','Aqua clip':'504',
            'Trigger':'Fresh airborne Jump/Circle after release; neutral or directional stick; once per airtime','Normal slot':10,'Olympus slot':10,
            'Native frames':40,'Directional input allowed':True,'Neutral stick required':False,'Normal falling clip':'506','Input restored after control':True,'Native gravity and velocity':True})
    for profile,report in enumerate(reports+[dodge]):
        for r in report['motions']:
            if not profile and r['normal_slot'] not in [101,102,103,104]:continue
            arc=d/'source_arcs'/r['source_bank']
            if not arc.exists():arc=ROOT/'capture_20261101/Sources/data/bbs/arc/pc'/r['source_bank']
            members,_=read_arc(arc.read_bytes())
            found=[]
            for member,data in members:
                if not data.startswith(b'PAM\0'):continue
                for a in read_pam(data,54):
                    if a.name!=r['donor']:continue
                    start=struct.unpack_from('<I',data,16+16*a.slot)[0]
                    actual_sha=hashlib.sha256(data[start:a.data_end]).hexdigest()
                    if r.get('source_sha256'):assert actual_sha==r['source_sha256'],(a.name,r['source_bank'])
                    found.append({'Ability':labels[profile] if profile<5 else 'all Aqua entries','Action':r['action'],'Normal slot':r['normal_slot'],
                        'Source name':a.name,'Source aliases':r.get('source_aliases',''),'Source bank':r['source_bank'],'PAM member':member,'Source frames':a.frame_count,'Source FPS':a.fps,
                        'Source frame range':str(r['source_range']) if r['source_range'] else 'full','Animation SHA256':hashlib.sha256(data[start:a.data_end]).hexdigest(),
                        'Native frames':r['native_frames'],'Native FPS':60})
            assert len(found)==1,(r['donor'],r['source_bank'],len(found));sources+=found
    for name,rows in [('ANIMATION_MAP.csv',maps),('AIR_DODGE_MAPPING.csv',airmaps),('TEST_CLIP_SOURCES.csv',sources)]:
        with (DEST/name).open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=list(rows[0]));w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
    expected={'version':12,'assets':[]}
    for name,actual in [('dll/kh1-aqua.dll',DEST/'dll/kh1-aqua.dll'),('xa_ex_0010.mset',DEST/'assets/xa_ex_0010.mset'),('xa_ex_0010_he.mset',DEST/'assets/xa_ex_0010_he.mset')]:
        expected['assets'].append({'name':name,'sha256':sha(actual),'bytes':actual.stat().st_size})
    (DEST/'expected_assets.json').write_text(json.dumps(expected,indent=2)+'\n')
    records=[r for report in reports+[dodge] for r in report['motions']]
    validation={'version':12,'test_round':4,'offline_checks_passed':True,'game_runtime_tested':False,
        'abilities':labels,'ability_ids':list(range(117,122)),'main_ground_finisher':'411','main_air_combo':['407','352','353'],'air_dodge':'504','normal_falling':'506',
        'test_4_combos':SETS,'air_aliases':AIR_ALIASES,'normal_motion_records_per_profile':47,'olympus_motion_records_per_profile':46,
        'unique_generated_pose_variants':len(records),'actual_pe_mock_tests':runtime['tests'],'geometry_assignment_tests':geometry['tests'],
        'pose_samples':sum(r['validated_pose_samples'] for r in records),'max_pose_position_fit_error':max(r['max_pose_position_error'] for r in records),
        'max_non_root_attachment_translation_error':max(r['max_non_root_attachment_translation_error'] for r in records),
        'max_scale_error':max(r['max_scale_error'] for r in records),'native_travel_error':max(r['root_helper_error'] for r in records),
        'original_motion_lengths_headers_counts_and_msets_preserved':True,'helper_slots':11,'left_palm_magic':206,
        'air_dodge_one_per_airtime':True,'air_dodge_directional_input_allowed':True,'air_dodge_neutral_stick_required':False,'air_dodge_extra_invulnerability':False,'dll_sha256':sha(DEST/'dll/kh1-aqua.dll'),
        'limitations':['Windows/KH1 execution and rendered appearance pending','Directional airborne Circle and new clips require in-game testing',
            '504 uses native fall gravity and40-frame timing; no added BBS travel or invulnerability','Thunder retains v10 alternate casting duration86/78']}
    (DEST/'validation.json').write_text(json.dumps(validation,indent=2)+'\n')
    with zipfile.ZipFile(DEST.with_suffix('.zip'),'w',zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED,compresslevel=9) as z:
        for p in sorted(DEST.rglob('*')):
            if p.is_file() and '__pycache__' not in p.parts:z.write(p,p.relative_to(DEST))
    print(json.dumps({'zip':str(DEST.with_suffix('.zip')),'bytes':DEST.with_suffix('.zip').stat().st_size,'sha256':sha(DEST.with_suffix('.zip')),'validation':validation},indent=2))
if __name__=='__main__':build()
